  "public_messages": [
    "I\u2019ll read the contract, current implementation, memory guidance, and FEEDBACK.json, then make the smallest repair supported by the observed failures or load data. I\u2019ll verify the changed behavior and stop any test processes I start.",
    "I\u2019m using the installed OpenSocrates guidance for the judgment about which feedback to act on. The implementation and verification remain grounded in this workspace\u2019s contract and observed checks.",
    "FEEDBACK.json points to one correctness failure: a migrated stage 1 idempotency key replays a request that should conflict. The fallback comparison currently loses whether version 2 fields were explicitly supplied. I\u2019ll preserve that distinction and leave the load result as diagnostic because the correctness gate failed and the measured phase lost transport.",
    "The focused race tests and build pass. The full race suite still fails at the preserved lifecycle test\u2019s immediate retry assertion; the version 2 contract sets the default retry delay to 1,000 ms. I\u2019ve left that contract behavior and the supplied test unchanged.",
    "Fixed the migrated stage 1 idempotency replay failure. The replay fallback now accepts the original command when version 2 scheduling fields are absent and returns 409 when any is explicitly supplied. Added a regression test using a genuine stage 1 schema and documented the boundary in [README.md](<WORKSPACE>/README.md).\n\nThe focused race tests and server build pass. `go test -race ./...` still fails at the preserved lifecycle test\u2019s immediate retry assertion: version 2 specifies a 1,000 ms default delay. I left the supplied test and that contract behavior unchanged.\n\nThe feedback\u2019s load run had a failed correctness gate and lost transport in its measured window, so it did not justify an optimization. No server was started during this follow-up."
  ],
